%!PS
% SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 EfterScript contributors
% SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
% backend: none
% oracle: skip the Flate encoding of an input is not unique across encoders; the printed bytes are this encoder's
% expect-output: 78012BC94855282CCD4CCE56482ACA2FCF5348CBAF0000478E0734>
% expect-output: the quick brown fox
% Scenario: FlateEncode writing through an ASCIIHexEncode filter to
% standard output: the zlib header 78 01 (deflate, 32K window, no
% dictionary, 0x7801 a multiple of 31), one final block (the low bits of
% 2B are 011: last block, fixed Huffman codes) holding the nineteen
% bytes, and the big-endian Adler-32 of the input, 478E0734. The text
% read back through FlateDecode gives the bytes.
% Expect: the hexadecimal text, then the decoded bytes.
(%stdout) (w) file /ASCIIHexEncode filter
<< /CloseTarget true >> /FlateEncode filter
dup (the quick brown fox) writestring closefile
(\n) print
<78012BC94855282CCD4CCE56482ACA2FCF5348CBAF0000478E0734> /FlateDecode filter
100 string readstring pop =
